# FDD 11 + 16 — Educator Credentialing / Application Processing. Phase 2 (FDD review)
# ingestion against the mied-v3 graph (11 domains now really converted, not just
# credentialing as in the earlier miedw-v2 pilot pass on this same FDD).
#
# Source: "11,16 - Educator Credentialing.docx" (FDD 11 + 16 combined). FDD 16's own
# folder ("16 - Educator credentialing - Application processing.docx") is confirmed a
# one-page pointer: its entire "Business Specifications" section reads "The business
# specifications for Epic 16 including the features 16.1-16.4 are covered under Epic 11
# 11,16 - Educator Credentialing.docx" — not separately modeled, per fdd-review
# CONVENTIONS.md's instruction to treat this pair as one ingestion.
#   - 26 embedded wireframe images (word/media/image1.png-image26.png) — same count as
#     the miedw-v2 pilot found.
#   - 73 review comments (word/comments.xml) — same set the pilot extracted, re-verified
#     independently in this pass (dated 2025-06-26 through 2026-03-27, MDE/CEPI product
#     owners Dontje/Groom/Chapman vs. vendor team Sinha/Punniyamoorthy/Caswell/Doherty).
#   - Tracked-change/comment threads corroborate that the visible .md text is a
#     mid-revision snapshot in a few places (11.1.1's Open/Attention-tabs concept was
#     replaced per comments #47/48 with a new, unattached wireframe; 11.1.2 was
#     corrected from Credential Number to Application Number per #56-58) — noted per
#     Requirement below rather than reconstructed as a diff.
#
# Two companion documents in FDD 11's own folder were also read in full, per this
# ingestion's brief, and both turned out to resolve real, previously-open questions:
#   - "Decision Sheet for Creating A Code in the Application Numbers.docx" — resolves
#     application_number generation (see Question_ApplicationNumberFormatResolved
#     below), and by contrast SHARPENS (does not resolve) credentialing-domain.ttl's
#     existing Question_CredentialNumberFormat, which is now updated in place there.
#   - "Interface Design document - MTTC EdReports (Pearson).docx" — resolves the
#     real-vs-aspirational status of "Pearson integration" referenced by FDD 11.8.1 (see
#     Question_MttcPearsonIntegrationRealityCheck below): it is a monthly manual file
#     pull from a Pearson website, not a live per-applicant API, and lines up exactly
#     with cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults already
#     modeled in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl.
# ("MiEdWorkforce-Bulk payments and Daily sub renewal.pdf", also in the folder, is a
# slide-deck-style walkthrough of the same 11.1.3 bulk-renewal-then-pay flow already
# covered by the FDD text and Wireframes 1-3 — skimmed, adds no new requirement or
# acceptance criterion beyond what's already modeled below, not separately cited.)
#
# Scope of this ingestion pass:
# - Granularity: the FDD's own Feature/User-Story numbering (11.1.1 ... 16.4.1 — 21 real
#   stories + 5 "this belongs to a different Business Specification/feature" pointer
#   notes: 11.3, 11.6, 11.7, 11.9, 16.3) is used as the Requirement unit, not the
#   separate "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS" table (53 rows, paraphrasing the same ~21 stories at
#   coarser granularity) earlier in the doc — modeling both would just duplicate the same
#   coverage under a second numbering scheme.
# - Comments: not all 73 modeled individually. ~15 near-identical "Define role" /
#   "Confirming if the role has been defined" threads recurring across nearly every
#   worklist/processing feature are consolidated into ONE Annotation
#   (Question_UndefinedProcessorRoles) — re-confirmed against mied-v3's own real iam/
#   conversion below: iam-domain.ttl mints zero sd:Role instances for any of these named
#   SOM Credentialing roles, so this is still a live, unresolved gap, not something the
#   real IAM conversion incidentally closed. A handful of other comments surfaced
#   genuinely distinct, substantive findings and are modeled individually below (the
#   Credential Removal Request agreement, the MTTC hard-block-vs-manual-review
#   contradiction, the Application-vs-Credential-Number correction).
# - Wireframes: image1.png-image8.png map to "Wireframe 1"-"Wireframe 8" (confirmed by
#   the miedw-v2 pilot's own direct-viewing pass — not re-verified here since the task
#   brief says that investigation doesn't need repeating). image9.png-image26.png (18
#   images) cluster under the "Wireframe 8" caption with no further captions — not
#   individually reviewed here either, same as the pilot; extracted fresh into this
#   file's own wireframes/ subfolder rather than referencing the pilot's copies.
#
# What's different from the miedw-v2 pilot (credentialing-only) pass, now that mied-v3
# has real conversions for documents/epp/profpractice/payments/iam:
# - Req_11_10_1 (view/download/export application documents) now links real
#   docs:Op_SearchDocuments/Op_DownloadDocument/Op_GetDocumentMetadata instead of the
#   pilot's placeholder-only docs:DocumentRetrievalOperation stub.
# - Req_11_2_1/11_2_2 (guidance-document tiles) now additionally cite
#   docs:Op_SearchDocuments/Op_DownloadDocument as the plausible underlying document
#   retrieval mechanism (Documents models category-scoped documents attached to an
#   arbitrary entity) — still a genuine gap on the credentialing side (no tile-specific,
#   role-gated "guidance category" listing endpoint), but a real partial improvement over
#   the pilot's "permission with nothing behind it at all" finding.
# - Req_16_4_1 (historical records) now cites real cross-domain operations —
#   epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments (enrollment info) and profp:Op_ListDisclosures/
#   Op_GetDisclosure (conviction info) — that didn't exist as real conversions when the
#   pilot ran. The core finding (no single consolidated "educator history" endpoint
#   spans all of these) still stands; it's now visibly a cross-domain aggregation gap
#   with named real gaps on each side, not a wholesale absence.
# - Req_11_5_1/Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance corroborated by the now-real
#   profp:Op_GetEducatorPprStatus (same operation credentialing's own v1/v2 stub for
#   GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance already anticipated verbatim).
# - Confirmed the "Pay Later" / "Unpaid Application Fees" queue gap (Req_11_1_3) is a
#   known, already-documented cross-domain gap, not a new one: payments-sequences.ttl's
#   own SequenceReference on `GET /applications/pending-payment?districtId=...` already
#   says "No such path in payments-api.yml" — this FDD's UX independently corroborates
#   that exact missing endpoint from the other side.
# - Confirmed the "Needs Responses" flag (Req_11_4_1) still does not exist anywhere in
#   the real profpractice-domain.ttl either (grepped, zero hits) — the gap the pilot
#   found (a flag distinct from ProfessionalPracticeStatus) is real and still unmodeled
#   on both sides of the credentialing/profpractices boundary, not just credentialing's.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix docs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:> .
@prefix epp:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:> .
@prefix profp: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:> .
@prefix pay:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:> .
@prefix iam:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:> .
@prefix dash:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:> .
@prefix mied:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:solution:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

cred:Fdd11_16Doc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/11 - Educator Credentialing/11,16 - Educator Credentialing.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers FDD Features 11.1-11.10 and 16.1-16.4. FDD 16's own separate .docx ('16 - Educator credentialing - Application processing.docx') is a one-page pointer to this combined document (confirmed by reading it: its Business Specifications section is a single sentence pointing here) — not separately modeled." .

cred:DecisionSheetAppNumbersDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "review" ;
    sd:section "abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/11 - Educator Credentialing/Decision Sheet for Creating A Code in the Application Numbers.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Dated 08/01/2024 decision record (MOECS/MiEdWorkforce product owners and QA) settling how CredentialApplication.application_number is generated going forward. Read in full for this ingestion per the task brief's instruction to check it against Question_CredentialNumberFormat." .

cred:MttcPearsonInterfaceDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
