#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 11.1: Temporary credential - Bulk renewal
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_1_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.1.1" ;
    sd:title "Permits landing page: search, renew, and manage permit applications" ;
    sd:statement "As a Business User with a Temporary Credential role, I want to view the Permits landing page so that I can search, renew, and manage permit applications." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Login and navigate to Home > Credential Management > Permits. Landing page has Open Applications and Closed Applications tabs (each showing counts). Search field supports partial match across Unique ID, Name, and Email with the standard hover text. Results table: Name, Email Address, UID, etc. User can filter on all columns and download results as Doc/Excel/Pdf. 'No results found' message shown/cleared per the standard eligibility-exclusion pattern." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListApplications ;
    sd:notes "Partial match only: cred:Op_ListApplications (generic GET /applications) has no Open/Closed tab concept, no Unique-ID/Name/Email combined search, and no Doc/Excel/Pdf export. Per comments #45-48, the Open/Applications-needing-Attention tab concept was itself revised mid-review ('the wireframe has been updated to remove the concept... new wireframe has been attached'), so this acceptance criteria may already be stale relative to the current (unattached) wireframe. See Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX (shared with 11.5.1/16.1.4) for the recurring search/export gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_1_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.1.2" ;
    sd:title "Application number as hyperlink to detailed credential view" ;
    sd:statement "As a Business User with a Temporary Credential role, I want the table on the Permits Page to display the Application number as a hyperlink, so that I can open a detailed view of the credential when necessary." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Application Number column displayed as a clickable hyperlink; clicking opens the detailed credential view page; Cancel returns to the Permits page." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_GetApplication ;
    sd:notes "Direct match: GET /applications/{applicationId} is exactly this. Comments #56-58 clarify this links via Application Number, not Credential Number, after an earlier draft confusion ('I'm confused... if the search here is referring to the screen above, then the column will have Application number as hyperlink and not the Credential number') — the acceptance criteria above already reflects the corrected version." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_1_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.1.3" ;
    sd:title "Bulk-select eligible educators and submit renewal applications at once" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce Business User with the Credential Application role, I want to select multiple eligible educators and submit their renewal applications at once, so that I can efficiently manage large volumes of permit renewals." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Dropdown on Permits landing page includes 'Renew Daily Substitutes' among several new-application options. Renewal landing page: eligibility text, partial-match search (Unique ID/Name/Email), results filtered to exclude actionable-PPR-flag records, checkbox multi-select, final price shown after selection, records with expired PPR shown but blocked from renewal (with notify-and-continue option), Review page with advisory + 3 attestation checkboxes, Submit, then a confirmation page offering 'Continue to Payment' or 'Pay Later' (moves applications to an 'Unpaid Application Fees' queue)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_InitiateBulkRenewals, cred:Seq_BulkRenewalInitiation ;
    sd:notes "Core bulk-submission flow matches Op_InitiateBulkRenewals/Seq_BulkRenewalInitiation well. Two confirmed gaps, both re-checked against the now-real cross-domain graphs: (1) the 3-checkbox attestation flow is richer than credentialing-technical-design.ttl's TP_ElectronicSignatureAttestationCapture (a single typed-name field) — see Question_ESignatureLegalSufficiency (already modeled in credentialing-technical-design.ttl), now also linked from here; (2) the 'Pay Later'/'Unpaid Application Fees' queue has no backing endpoint anywhere — payments-sequences.ttl's OWN SequenceReference on `GET /applications/pending-payment?districtId=...` already says 'No such path in payments-api.yml', independently corroborating this exact gap from the Payments side, not just Credentialing's. Per comments #62/63, this story was agreed to need splitting from a 'new permit application' story that got tangled into the same acceptance criteria — the acceptance criteria above already isolates the renewal-specific parts." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 11.2: Landing pages
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_2_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.2.1" ;
    sd:title "Temporary Credential guidance documents on dashboard" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce user with the Business user/Temporary Credential role, I want Temporary Credential guidance documents to be available on the dashboard, so that I can easily access relevant information." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Dashboard shows a 'Temporary Credential Guidance' tile, restricted to the Business User/Temporary Credential role, listing all guidance docs defined by the Credentialing Admin; each is viewable/previewable and downloadable as PDF; 'No guidance documents available' message when empty." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Perm_GuidanceView, docs:Op_SearchDocuments, docs:Op_DownloadDocument ;
    sd:notes "cred:Perm_GuidanceView exists but has no backing ApiOperation or Sequence in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl. Documents' now-real category-scoped document model (docs:DocumentCategoryAggregate, docs:Op_SearchDocuments/Op_DownloadDocument, both internal-service — meant to be called by another domain's own backend, exactly this shape) is a genuinely plausible underlying mechanism, an improvement on the pilot's finding of nothing at all behind this permission — but no credentialing-owned endpoint composes them into a role-gated 'guidance tile' list, and no 'guidance' DocumentCategory instance is declared anywhere. Per comment #70 (Punniyamoorthy: 'the download, view/open is outside the scope of MiEd' since the guidance documents live in Documents capability) this split is intentional, similar to the existing PDF-generation split with TP_CertificatePdfGeneration. Not fully resolved here — see Question_GuidanceDocumentTileGap below." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_2_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.2.2" ;
    sd:title "Certificate guidance documents on dashboard (Citizen)" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce Citizen user, I want Certificate guidance documents to be available on the dashboard, so that I can easily access relevant information." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Dashboard shows a 'Certificate Guidance' tile, Citizen-only, listing all Certificate guidance docs; each viewable/openable and downloadable; must work on desktop and mobile; empty-state message." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Perm_GuidanceView, docs:Op_SearchDocuments, docs:Op_DownloadDocument ;
    sd:notes "Same gap as 11.2.1 — Wireframe5 (the Citizen 'I Want to' home page) shows a 'Certification Guidance Documents' button matching this story, but no backing endpoint composes the role-gated tile. Comments #72/73 debated whether the empty-state message is even a real requirement ('I don't think there will be a scenario where there will be no guidance documents' / 'There could be a lapse... upon implementation or when being reviewed') — resolved in favor of keeping it." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.3" ;
    sd:title "Historical Data (feature-level pointer)" ;
    sd:statement "All user stories regarding the Business and Admin users' ability to view the citizen user's historical data can be found within the user stories associated with other features in this FDD." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Seq_ViewDefinitionHistory ;
    sd:notes "Self-referential pointer within the same FDD, not a standalone requirement — content lives in 11.5's 'view applicant's current and historical data' story and 16.4's Historical Records feature. Cross-referenced for completeness, not double-counted as its own gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 11.4: Professional practice review
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_4_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.4.1" ;
    sd:title "Renewal search filtered by PPR and Needs-Responses flags" ;
    sd:statement "As a Business User, I want the Renewal and Bulk Renewal search to display only Daily Substitute Permit records that meet the eligibility criteria based on the PPR and Needs Responses flags, so that I can identify and renew only those permits that are eligible for processing." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "System checks PPR flag and Needs Responses flag per permit during a renewal search. Includes: Needs Responses = N AND (no PPR flag OR non-actionable PPR flag). Excludes: actionable PPR flag AND Needs Responses = Y." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance ;
    sd:notes "Genuine coverage gap, re-confirmed against the now-real profpractice-domain.ttl (grepped for 'Needs Responses'/'NeedsResponse': zero hits): 'Needs Responses' is a distinct flag from ProfessionalPracticeStatus (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked) and exists in neither credentialing-domain.ttl's CredentialApplication/IssuedCredential model NOR profpractice's own real DisclosureAggregate/EducatorPPRStatusAggregate model — this FDD's PPR-flag-plus-Needs-Responses-flag combination is more granular than what either domain's real conversion has modeled, on both sides of the boundary." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 11.5: Worklist, Admin Pages
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_5_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.5.1" ;
    sd:title "Auto-approve or route credential applications to the correct worklist" ;
    sd:statement "As the MiEdWorkforce system, I want to automatically approve credential applications or route them to the appropriate worklist based on business rules, so that applications are processed efficiently and consistently without manual intervention." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Evaluate every submission against eligibility rules (PPR flags, Needs Responses, MTTC scores, expiration status, renewal count, academic year, in/out-of-state, payment, other Business Rule Management rules). If met: auto-approve, auto-issue, no worklist task, confirmation email. If not: route to the correct worklist (Permits/Career Authorization, Special Education, Educator Standard/Professional, School Nurse, School Administrator, Additional Endorsements, Renewal License, Candidate Tracking) by credential type/status/PPR/Needs-Responses; create a worklist task for the Citizen to fill out PPR when applicable. Each worklist has its own defined search filters and result columns." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria, cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering, cred:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval, profp:Op_GetEducatorPprStatus ;
    sd:notes "The routing/auto-approve LOGIC matches Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria/Rule_ManualReviewTriggering/Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval closely, and the PPR-flag check is now corroborated by a real cross-domain operation: profp:Op_GetEducatorPprStatus IS the same GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance credentialing's own Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance already stubbed as profp:PPRClearanceOperation (profpractice-api.ttl reuses that exact IRI verbatim) — a genuine corroboration the pilot pass couldn't make with profpractices still a stub. The discrete NAMED worklists with per-type search filters/result columns remain a separate, unmodeled UX layer — see Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX. Wireframe6/Wireframe7 are the visual evidence for this gap: real filter fields (Has conviction?, Use alternative pass, SSN) and an MTTC Information sub-panel with no corresponding ApiOperation anywhere. This also directly corroborates Question_WorklistAssignmentScope (credentialing-domain.ttl, Open Question #34) — the FDD independently describes real, named, filterable worklists, not just 'anyone holding the approve permission for this scope.'" ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_5_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.5.2" ;
    sd:title "Suspend or revoke a certificate/credential (valid or expired)" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce Credential Administrator, I want to suspend or revoke a certificate, credential (whether valid or expired), so that I can enforce compliance, address violations, and manage educator credential statuses appropriately." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Credential Administrator role only. Works on Valid and Expired. Admin enters a reason (predefined or free text) and may notify educator/employing districts. Status updates immediately across worklists/dashboards/profile. Audit entry: Username/ID, Date/time, Previous Status, New Status. Suspended/Revoked items unusable for any credentialing function. Confirmation message shown." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SuspendCredential, cred:Op_RevokeCredential, cred:Seq_SuspendOrRevokeCredential, cred:Rule_CredentialStatusTransitions ;
    sd:notes "Strong direct match on the core action. 'Suspend/revoke EXPIRED credentials' is new detail — cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate's invariants only explicitly discuss Valid credentials being suspended/revoked; extending to Expired is consistent with the existing state model (Expired is not terminal) but wasn't explicitly called out before. Reason-capture and notify-district are not modeled as distinct fields anywhere; minor gap, folded into this note rather than a separate Annotation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_5_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.5.3" ;
    sd:title "Nullify an endorsement (valid or expired)" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce Credential Administrator, I want to nullify an endorsement (whether valid or expired), so that I can permanently invalidate endorsements that were issued in error or violate requirements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Credential Administrator role only. Applies to endorsements, not certificates directly. Nullified endorsements cannot be reactivated (re-application required). System should warn or prevent nullification that would leave a certificate with zero endorsements (unless the certificate type allows it). Status updates immediately; audit entry as above; educator and district notified." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_NullifyEndorsement, cred:Seq_NullifyEndorsement ;
    sd:notes "Good direct match on the core action. Genuine gap: the 'warn or prevent zero-endorsement certificates' rule is a new invariant not present on cred:IssuedEndorsementAggregate or cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate today." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_5_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.5.4" ;
    sd:title "Admin submits a credential application on behalf of a Citizen User" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce Credential Administrator, I want to submit a credential application on behalf of a Citizen User, so that I can process necessary credentials for educators who cannot access the system or rectify administrative errors while ensuring the application passes through standard system validations." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Admin selects a citizen user, clicks Add Certificate, application still runs the full business-rule validation (eligibility, endorsement matching, academic year, coursework, validity period, MTTC) — cannot save if rules fail, with clear error messages. Admin can add/edit/save internal remarks (predefined templates or free text), not visible to Citizen/Business users. Action recorded in audit history including timestamp, certificate type, rule validations applied, and remarks." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Perm_ApplicationManualSubmit ;
    sd:notes "Strong, previously-missing corroboration re-confirmed in mied-v3: cred:Perm_ApplicationManualSubmit's own notes already say 'for bulk data entry, historical corrections, or single-application submission on behalf of an educator who cannot access the system (application still passes through standard validations — not a bypass)' — almost verbatim what this story describes — but no single-application ApiOperation or Sequence exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl (only cred:Op_InitiateBulkRenewals for the bulk path; no 'Op_InitiateApplication'-style single-admin-submit endpoint was added between the pilot pass and this one). Real, still-undetected-in-code coverage gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 11.6/11.7: deferred to other Business Specifications
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.6" ;
    sd:title "Email/Communication (feature-level pointer)" ;
    sd:statement "All underlying logic for sending, tracking, and displaying emails, alerts and notifications are derived from Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these tools specifically for the Educator Credentialing module." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Email/communication behavior is explicitly owned by Business Specification #6 (Communications), not Credentialing. Consistent with comm:CommunicationsContext already being a real conversion that subscribes to Credentialing's own events." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_11_6 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.7" ;
    sd:title "Dashboard (feature-level pointer)" ;
    sd:statement "All underlying logic for the display, organization, and rendering of the dashboard is derived from Business Specification #3 (Dashboards). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these elements specifically for the Educator Credentialing workflow." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Dashboard rendering is owned by Business Specification #3 (Dashboards) — dash:DashboardsContext (declared centrally in mied-v3/solution.ttl, still sd:status \"stub\": no FDD in mied-v3's 11-domain scope covers it yet). Comments #67-69 confirm at least one requirement was actively moved out of this FDD into the Dashboards spec during review ('This requirement should be moved to #3 dashboards')." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_11_7 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 11.8: MTTC Verification
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_8_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.8.1" ;
    sd:title "Automatically reference an educator's stored MTTC score(s) on endorsement selection" ;
    sd:statement "As a System, I must automatically reference an educator's stored MTTC score(s) when they select an endorsement during a credential application, so that the correct test results are associated with the requested subject area without manual data entry." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Retrieve Test Code(s) from Business Rule Management's Endorsement-to-Test-Code mapping. Search the MTTC Data Store (populated via Pearson integration) by Unique ID (or SSN) + Test Code. Link the most recent passing score. If multiple tests map to one endorsement and 'All Tests Required' is active, verify status for all required codes." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation, cred:AssessmentResultAggregate, cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults ;
    sd:notes "The AND/OR combination logic on EndorsementDefinition.RequiredAssessments matches the 'All Tests Required' flag concept well. The Pearson-integration reality-check is now RESOLVED by reading the Interface Design document (see Question_MttcPearsonIntegrationRealityCheck below): 'the MTTC Data Store (populated via Pearson integration)' this story describes is, concretely, cred:AssessmentResultAggregate records populated by cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults — an admin manually downloads a monthly fixed-width file from a Pearson website (per the interface doc, 'Incoming File (Prod & Test): N/A (manual process today)') and bulk-imports it. There is no live per-applicant query against Pearson itself; 'populated via Pearson integration' describes this monthly manual-import pipeline, matching credentialing-domain.md's own 'Data Source (Current State): manual entry from uploaded score reports' almost exactly." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_8_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.8.2" ;
    sd:title "Use MTTC score status to validate eligibility and gate submission" ;
    sd:statement "As a System, I must use the referenced MTTC score status to validate eligibility against Business Rules, so that I can automatically prevent the issuance of credentials to unqualified candidates or flag them for review." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "If a passing MTTC score is required and none is on file, block submission with an error (not: flag after submission). If the endorsement requires no test (e.g. certain World Languages), bypass score validation. If no passing score for a Temporary Credential, dynamically present alternative eligibility questions per the Business Rule Management decision tree. If all criteria including MTTC pass, mark eligible for Auto-Approval." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation, cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria ;
    sd:notes "Real contradiction, not just a gap: credentialing-domain.ttl's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering lists 'required assessment results missing or failing' as a condition that flags an application for MANUAL REVIEW after submission. This FDD's own comment thread (#120 Punniyamoorthy: 'There is no need to flag the application for missing/fail MTTC score as the system will not allow the applicant to proceed to submit the application without the passing test score' / #121 Dontje: 'Agree') establishes the opposite: missing/failing MTTC should HARD-BLOCK submission, never reach manual review at all. See Question_ManualReviewVsHardBlockForMttc below — a genuine disagreement between two source documents, not resolved here." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_11_8_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.8.3" ;
    sd:title "View detailed MTTC test history within the application review screen" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Administrator or Credential Processor, I want to view the detailed MTTC test history for an applicant within the application review screen, so that I can verify they have passed the specific tests required for the requested endorsements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "'MTTC Information' section: Test Name, Test Code, Status (Passed/Failed), Date Passed, Exam Date. Highlight endorsements whose required test code has no 'Passed' status. Viewable even for tests taken prior to the current application." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: no ApiOperation or Sequence exposes this view anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl. Wireframe7 shows exactly this 'MTTC Information' table with the same columns the acceptance criteria lists — strong visual confirmation the requirement is real and specific, not speculative. Genuine coverage gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No ApiOperation or Sequence exposes an 'MTTC Information' review view anywhere in the graph, despite Wireframe7 showing exactly this screen (Test Name/Test Code/Status/Date Passed/Exam Date columns) as a real, designed feature." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_11_8_3 ; sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirement — Feature 11.9: Identity Management Integration (pending upstream)
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_9 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.9" ;
    sd:title "Identity Management Integration (feature-level pointer, pending)" ;
    sd:statement "User stories for this feature are currently pending and will be developed upon completion of the related business specification, User Management - Identity Management Integration (15)." ;
    sd:status "pending" ;
    sd:notes "Not a gap in Credentialing's own modeling — the FDD itself says this can't be written yet because an upstream spec (FDD 15) isn't finished. Tracked here so it doesn't silently disappear from the coverage picture; revisit once FDD 15 exists. Note: iam-domain.ttl is now a real conversion, but it documents IAM's OWN identity-matching/authorization model (Mi-Key, near-match resolution, etc.), not the specific FDD-15 user stories this pointer awaits — so this remains genuinely pending, not incidentally resolved by IAM's real conversion existing." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:questioning ;
    rdfs:comment "Feature 11.9 (Identity Management Integration) has no user stories yet — blocked on FDD 15 (User Management - Identity Management Integration) being finished first. Not a Credentialing-side gap; revisit once FDD 15 exists." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_11_9 ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirement — Feature 11.10: Document Upload
#################################################################

cred:Req_11_10_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "11.10.1" ;
    sd:title "View, download, and export supporting documents on a credential application" ;
    sd:statement "As a user with the Credential Applications role, I want to view, download, and export supporting documents uploaded to a credential application, so that I can verify the applicant's eligibility and ensure all requirements are met before approving or denying the request." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "List of uploaded documents with metadata (File Name, File Type/Size, Upload Date, Uploaded By). View/Download in PDF, PNG, or JPEG." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy docs:Op_SearchDocuments, docs:Op_GetDocumentMetadata, docs:Op_DownloadDocument ;
    sd:notes "Real improvement over the miedw-v2 pilot pass, which could only cite a placeholder-named docs:DocumentRetrievalOperation stub (documents wasn't a real conversion yet). Documents' now-real API models exactly this shape: docs:Op_SearchDocuments (list by attachment), docs:Op_GetDocumentMetadata (file name/size/upload metadata — docs:DocumentAggregate's own invariants explicitly preserve original filename in metadata), docs:Op_DownloadDocument (SAS-token download). Remaining gap: docs:DocumentAggregate's own metadata doesn't appear to carry an explicit 'Uploaded By' user-identity field in its stored value objects (docs:MalwareScanResultVO/BlobReference/RetentionPolicyVO/LegalHoldVO) — worth confirming whether that's tracked via docs:DocumentAccessLog instead; and no dedicated 'export' (as opposed to plain download) operation or PNG/JPEG-specific handling is called out. Minor, folded into this note rather than a separate Annotation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 16.1: Pending Credential Application Review & Process
#################################################################

cred:Req_16_1_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.1.1" ;
    sd:title "Route applications to the correct worklist" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Processor I want applications to be routed to the correct worklist so that they can be reviewed by the appropriate team." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Assign to the sub-worklist matching Credential Type (Certificates/Permits/Career Authorizations/Special Education Approvals). If PPR Admin Flag = On, place in 'PPR Hold' status regardless of other criteria. Assign to exactly one active worklist; update the assignment automatically on status change; display the assigned worklist on the application details screen." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering, cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance ;
    sd:notes "'Assign to exactly one ACTIVE worklist' and 'display the assigned worklist on the application' is the clearest FDD-level statement yet that discrete, named worklist assignment is real product behavior — directly reinforcing Question_WorklistAssignmentScope (credentialing-domain.ttl, Open Question #34) and Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX below. Strong corroboration of an existing finding, not a new one." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_16_1_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.1.2" ;
    sd:title "Auto-approve eligible applications" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Processor I want eligible applications to be auto approved so that certificates can be issued without manual intervention." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Evaluate Business Rule Management eligibility on submission; auto-approve and auto-issue if met; no worklist task created; record approval in the audit log." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria, cred:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval ;
    sd:notes "Direct match, no gaps identified." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_16_1_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.1.3" ;
    sd:title "Require manual review when eligibility rules fail" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Processor I want applications to require manual review so that incorrect certificates are not issued." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Block auto-approval when any eligibility rule fails; assign to a review worklist; display ineligibility reasons to authorized users; do not issue until explicit approval." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering, cred:Seq_ApplicationManualReviewAndApproval ;
    sd:notes "Direct match. Per comment #127 (Punniyamoorthy: 'ineligible applications - doesn't sound right, applications that do not meet auto-approval are sent to worklist for review. If they are not eligible then system should have stopped them from submission' / Dontje: 'Agree') the FDD's own wording was corrected during review — 'require manual review' means 'didn't qualify for the fast path,' not 'is ineligible to exist as an application' — consistent with how Rule_ManualReviewTriggering is already modeled, no change needed here." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_16_1_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.1.4" ;
    sd:title "Search and view credential worklists" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Processor I want to search and view credential worklists so that I can locate applications efficiently." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Search filters specific to each worklist type (Permit/Career Authorization/Special Education Approvals; Certificate), filterable per column, sortable, hyperlinked application numbers, 'No results found' empty state, downloadable as Word/Excel/Pdf." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: same structural gap as 11.1.1/11.5.1 — see Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "Three FDD user stories (11.1.1, 11.5.1, 16.1.4) each independently describe discrete, named, per-credential-type worklist search screens with their own filter sets and result columns, plus a recurring 'download results as Word/Excel/Pdf' export capability. Nothing in credentialing-api.ttl models per-worklist-type search (only the generic Op_ListApplications) or any export format at all. Wireframes 4/6/7 are visual evidence this is a real, designed UI, not a speculative wish-list item. Consolidated into one Annotation rather than three near-duplicates since it's the same underlying gap." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_11_1_1, cred:Req_11_5_1, cred:Req_16_1_4 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 16.2: Assigning Certificate Status
#################################################################

cred:Req_16_2_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.2.1" ;
    sd:title "Update application status through the workflow" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Processor I want to update the status of an application so that it reflects its current position in the workflow." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Allow status updates to predefined values (Submitted, Approved, Denied, On Hold, and others per credentialing-domain.md's fuller state list). Restrict by role. Log all changes (timestamp, User ID, previous/current status) under a History tab. Display current status on the application summary page." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ApproveApplication, cred:Op_DenyApplication ;
    sd:notes "Approve/Deny are covered; 'On Hold' is not — this is the exact same gap credentialing-permissions.ttl's own notes already flagged on cred:Perm_ApplicationPlaceHold ('no API operation exists for this permission yet') and credentialing-sequences.ttl's own SequenceReference on the same `POST /applications/{id}/on-hold` call (resolutionStatus \"no-such-endpoint\"), both still true in mied-v3. This FDD story is independent, later confirmation of the same known gap, not a new one." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_16_2_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.2.2" ;
    sd:title "Enter internal comments for staff collaboration" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Administrator I want to enter internal comments so that internal staff can collaborate." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Free-form editing; visibility restricted to authorized users; deletable by admins; audit history (Modified By, Modified On)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:ApplicationProcessingNotes ;
    sd:notes "Matches cred:ApplicationProcessingNotes (DomainEntity: 'Internal comments from credential processors, attached to an application'). This FDD's generic 'restricted to authorized users' is consistent with, not more specific than, credentialing's existing access-gating notes on that entity." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Req_16_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.3" ;
    sd:title "Email/Communication (feature-level pointer)" ;
    sd:statement "All underlying logic for sending, tracking, and displaying emails, alerts and notifications are derived from Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these tools specifically for the Educator Credentialing module." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Same deferral to Communications as Req_11_6, repeated verbatim for the 16.x feature set." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_16_3 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirement — Feature 16.4: Historical Records
#################################################################

cred:Req_16_4_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "16.4.1" ;
    sd:title "View historical records" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Processor I want to view historical records so that I can make informed decisions." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Clicking a Username hyperlink displays current and historical certificates, permits and endorsements, uploaded documents, enrollment and conviction data, and Demographic/Employment/Education information. Access restricted by role. Data retained per the State Retention Policy." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments, profp:Op_ListDisclosures, docs:Op_SearchDocuments ;
    sd:notes "No single consolidated 'educator history' view/endpoint exists anywhere across the graph — that core finding from the miedw-v2 pilot pass still stands, but it is now visible as a NAMED cross-domain aggregation gap rather than a wholesale absence, now that epp/profpractices/documents are real conversions: epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments (enrollment info), profp:Op_ListDisclosures (conviction/disclosure info), docs:Op_SearchDocuments (uploaded documents) are each real, individually-callable operations that WOULD need to be composed by a single 'view educator history' screen — no such composing operation/sequence exists in credentialing, epp, profpractices, or documents today. Demographic/Employment/Education information isn't clearly owned by any of these four domains either (iam holds identity-matching data, not employment/education history) — see Question_HistoricalRecordsCompositionGap below. The 'State Retention Policy' reference is new and doesn't correspond to anything in the graph — captured as a Solution-level NFR below rather than invented as a credentialing-specific rule, per this project's convention of attaching NFRs at the sd:Solution root." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

mied:MiEdWorkforce sd:nonFunctionalRequirement "Data covered by 'historical records' views (certificates, permits, endorsements, documents, enrollment, conviction, demographic/employment/education info) must be retained per the State of Michigan's State Retention Policy (FDD 11,16, Feature 16.4.1). The specific retention schedule/duration isn't stated in this FDD — see Question_StateRetentionPolicyUndefined." .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:questioning ;
    rdfs:comment "What is the actual State Retention Policy schedule referenced by Feature 16.4.1 — how long must historical educator records be retained, and does it vary by record type (certificates vs. conviction data vs. demographic info)? Not stated anywhere in this FDD." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_16_4_1 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No operation or sequence composes a single 'view educator history' screen across the four-plus domains this FDD story spans (credentialing certificates/permits/endorsements, documents uploaded files, epp enrollment, profpractices conviction/disclosure data, plus demographic/employment/education info not clearly owned anywhere). Each underlying per-domain operation now exists for real (epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments, profp:Op_ListDisclosures, docs:Op_SearchDocuments) — the gap is specifically the missing aggregation/composition layer, not the absence of underlying data access." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_16_4_1 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

#################################################################
# Cross-cutting Annotations derived from the docx review-comment thread
#################################################################

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
    rdfs:comment "Recurring, still-unresolved thread (at least 15 separate comments across 2025-06-26 through 2026-03-23, spanning Dontje/MDE, Groom/CEPI, Sinha/DTMB-Contractor, Caswell/DTMB-Contractor) asking who exactly holds each 'SOM Credentialing ___' / worklist-processor / guidance-manager role this FDD keeps leaving as a blank ('Define role', 'Confirming if the role has been defined'). As of the last comment on this thread (Groom, 2026-03-23): 'Need help with refining and giving more definition around user role/functions for this area' — i.e. still open at the time of this ingestion. Re-checked against mied-v3's now-real iam-domain.ttl: it models Role as a UbiquitousTerm concept ('user-facing bundled permissions... e.g. Staffing Administrator, Credential Processor') but mints ZERO actual sd:Role instances anywhere in the graph (grepped iam/*.ttl and credentialing/*.ttl for 'a sd:Role': no hits) — so this is not a gap the real IAM conversion incidentally closed; the underlying role catalog this FDD keeps deferring to still doesn't exist as data anywhere in mied-v3, only as permission definitions (Perm_ApplicationApprove/.Deny/.PlaceHold, Perm_GuidanceManage, etc.) that were never reconciled against named roles in either the FDD text or IAM's own conversion." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_11_2_1, cred:Req_11_5_1, cred:Req_16_1_1, cred:Perm_ApplicationApprove, cred:Perm_GuidanceManage ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "contradiction" ;
    rdfs:comment "credentialing-domain.ttl's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering lists missing/failing required assessment results as a condition that flags an application for MANUAL REVIEW after submission. This FDD's own review comments (#120 Punniyamoorthy / #121 Dontje, 'Agree') establish instead that the system should hard-block SUBMISSION itself when a required MTTC score is missing or failing — manual review should never be reached for this specific cause. Two source documents disagree on where in the pipeline this check belongs; not resolved here." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering, cred:Req_11_8_2 ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .

cred:Question_MttcPearsonIntegrationRealityCheck a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "discrepancy" ;
    rdfs:comment "RESOLVED by reading 'Interface Design document - MTTC EdReports (Pearson).docx' in full for this ingestion pass, per the task brief's instruction. Prior state: FDD Feature 11.8.1 describes 'the MTTC Data Store (populated via Pearson integration)' as an already-established, per-applicant-queryable data source, while credentialing-domain.md's AssessmentResult aggregate describes the current state as manual entry from uploaded score reports, with Pearson API integration listed only as a 'Data Source (Future State)' possibility. The interface document settles which is accurate: it specifies a monthly (Frequency: Monthly, Data Volume: 4MB/month), one-way-receive (Data Direction: 'One way receive'), HTTPS GET file download from a Pearson-hosted website — explicitly still 'Incoming File (Prod & Test): N/A (manual process today)' as of the document's own text. There is no live, synchronous, per-applicant Pearson API — 'the MTTC Data Store' is exactly cred:AssessmentResultAggregate as populated by the existing cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults manual-bulk-import flow (an admin downloads Pearson's monthly file and uploads it via credentialing.assessment-result.import), consistent with — not contradicting — credentialing-domain.md's 'Current State' description. asp:AssessmentProviderSystem's existing sd:hasApi false is therefore CONFIRMED correct, not stale. FDD 11.8.1's phrasing ('populated via Pearson integration') is real but describes this batch-file pipeline, not a live query; worth flagging to the FDD's own authors that 'integration' reads as more automated than the interface spec they themselves wrote actually describes." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:AssessmentResultAggregate, cred:Req_11_8_1 ;
    sd:resolutionNotes "Confirmed via Interface Design document - MTTC EdReports (Pearson).docx (abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/11 - Educator Credentialing/): monthly manual file download, not a live API; existing cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/Seq_ImportAssessmentResults modeling is accurate and needs no change." ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc, cred:MttcPearsonInterfaceDoc .

cred:Question_ApplicationNumberFormatResolved a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
    rdfs:comment "Reading 'Decision Sheet for Creating A Code in the Application Numbers.docx' in full for this ingestion pass RESOLVES a related-but-distinct open question the domain doc's Open Question #35 doesn't directly ask: how is CredentialApplication.application_number (distinct from IssuedCredential.credential_number) generated? Decision made 08/01/2024 (Option 3, preferred): two alpha-prefixed identifiers, TXXXXXX (Temporary) and CXXXXXX (Certifications), each with its own incrementing-integer generator starting at 1, unpadded, capped at 6 digits, extending/resetting the scheme to be determined if the threshold is reached. This directly informs cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's application_number field/generation rule, which nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl currently documents. IMPORTANT: this decision does NOT resolve Question_CredentialNumberFormat (credentialing-domain.ttl, Open Question #35) — that question is specifically about IssuedCredential.credential_number, whose own documented examples ('PV0000000772064', 'CC-K46940078990') don't match the TXXXXXX/CXXXXXX scheme this decision describes at all (different length, different prefix conventions, no relation to the T/C temporary-vs-certificate split). See Question_CredentialNumberFormat's updated resolutionNotes (credentialing-domain.ttl) for how this sharpens rather than closes that question." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate ;
    sd:resolutionNotes "application_number generation is now documented: TXXXXXX/CXXXXXX prefix + unpadded incrementing integer per type, per the 08/01/2024 Decision Sheet. credential_number (a different field on a different aggregate) remains unresolved — see Question_CredentialNumberFormat." ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc, cred:DecisionSheetAppNumbersDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "Comment #38 (Sinha, 2025-11-12): 'Can we add a point for Credential Removal Request?' — Comment #39 (Dontje, 2026-03-02): '@Sinha, Yashi (DTMB-Contractor) Yes, please add the new requirement.' The product owner agreed to add a 'Credential Removal Request' capability, distinct from Suspend/Revoke/Nullify (all administrative actions on an existing credential's status, not a request to remove/delete one outright). No corresponding user story, acceptance criteria, or Requirement instance exists anywhere in the current FDD text — the agreement was made in a comment but never drafted into the document itself. A genuine 'agreed but not yet written' gap, distinct from an ordinary coverage gap. Still true in mied-v3: no Op_RemoveCredential/Op_DeleteIssuedCredential-style operation exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Rule_CredentialStatusTransitions ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:owner "MDE (Dontje) / DTMB (Sinha)" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd11_16Doc .
